WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.734 --> 00:00:08.540
Annie was excited, along with everyone else in her class.

2
00:00:08.541 --> 00:00:13.617
The children were getting ready to start rehearsing for their annual play.

3
00:00:13.618 --> 00:00:18.689
This year the play was The Three Billy Goats Gruff.

4
00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:26.761
Their teacher, Ms. Fisher, had been reading the story to them for weeks now, and they all knew it by heart.

5
00:00:26.762 --> 00:00:29.752
Everyone wanted to be in the play.

6
00:00:29.753 --> 00:00:33.364
Everyone, that is, except Henry.

7
00:00:33.365 --> 00:00:39.766
"I just want to stand in the corner and be a tree," Henry told Annie.

8
00:00:39.767 --> 00:00:45.841
"Come on, Henry! Being in a play will be fun!" Annie said.

9
00:00:45.842 --> 00:00:51.427
Ms. Fisher tried to get the children to quiet down.

10
00:00:51.428 --> 00:00:54.339
"I need everyone to listen!

11
00:00:54.340 --> 00:00:57.690
We're going to have our first rehearsal now.

12
00:00:57.691 --> 00:01:00.546
Who knows what a rehearsal is?"

13
00:01:00.547 --> 00:01:02.825
Annie raised her hand.

14
00:01:02.826 --> 00:01:06.412
"It's when we practice for the play."

15
00:01:06.413 --> 00:01:17.088
"Yes, Annie. This year, everyone is going to have a speaking part, so we have to practice saying our lines," said Ms. Fisher.

16
00:01:17.089 --> 00:01:20.863
"Nobody will stand around as a tree.

17
00:01:20.864 --> 00:01:22.489
There are four parts:

18
00:01:22.490 --> 00:01:28.518
the first goat, the second goat, the third goat, and the troll.

19
00:01:28.519 --> 00:01:31.303
Everyone will share a part.

20
00:01:31.304 --> 00:01:35.109
I've already chosen who will play what."

21
00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:41.603
Someone called out, "I know what Henry is going to be—the troll!"

22
00:01:41.604 --> 00:01:45.347
All the children laughed except Annie.

23
00:01:45.348 --> 00:01:51.001
"No, I'm not!" yelled Henry, as he ran under a table.

24
00:01:51.002 --> 00:01:55.159
"I don't want to be in a stupid play!"

25
00:01:55.160 --> 00:02:03.382
Ms. Fisher said patiently, "Henry, if you stay under that table, you'll miss our first rehearsal.

26
00:02:03.383 --> 00:02:05.484
Then you can't be in the play.

27
00:02:05.485 --> 00:02:07.812
Don't you want to join us?"

28
00:02:07.813 --> 00:02:10.601
Henry shook his head.

29
00:02:10.602 --> 00:02:15.418
"Okay, then you will sit in the corner and watch us.

30
00:02:15.419 --> 00:02:17.155
You know where to go,"

31
00:02:17.156 --> 00:02:21.215
said Ms. Fisher, pointing to a chair in the corner of the room.

32
00:02:21.216 --> 00:02:25.782
Henry sat in the chair and sadly watched the rest of the class.

33
00:02:25.783 --> 00:02:29.476
Annie was chosen to be one of the first goats.

34
00:02:29.477 --> 00:02:32.149
She wanted to make Henry feel better.

35
00:02:32.150 --> 00:02:34.109
She tried smiling at him.

36
00:02:34.110 --> 00:02:36.347
But he didn't look at her.

37
00:02:36.348 --> 00:02:40.754
Later, during lunch, Annie tried talking to Henry.

38
00:02:40.755 --> 00:02:44.080
But he ignored her for the rest of the day.

39
00:02:44.081 --> 00:02:48.031
He didn't care if he had to sit in the corner during every rehearsal.

40
00:02:48.032 --> 00:02:51.013
He would not be in the play.

41
00:02:51.014 --> 00:02:55.000
The next day, the class rehearsed again.

42
00:02:55.001 --> 00:03:02.435
The goats were practicing walking over the bridge while saying, "Trip, trap, trip, trap."

43
00:03:02.436 --> 00:03:06.485
But Ms. Fisher wasn't pleased.

44
00:03:06.486 --> 00:03:11.238
She said, "Something is missing.

45
00:03:11.239 --> 00:03:14.885
We need to make the goats' footsteps louder.

46
00:03:14.886 --> 00:03:19.080
Each goat should sound heavier than the one before it.

47
00:03:19.081 --> 00:03:23.366
We'll have to think of something."

48
00:03:23.367 --> 00:03:29.650
Meanwhile, Annie was trying to think of how to make Henry interested in the play.

49
00:03:29.651 --> 00:03:32.456
The kids had music class next.

50
00:03:32.457 --> 00:03:36.289
They were all allowed to choose their instruments.

51
00:03:36.290 --> 00:03:38.481
Annie chose the tambourine.

52
00:03:38.482 --> 00:03:41.067
Henry chose the drum.

53
00:03:41.068 --> 00:03:45.289
They paraded around the room with their instruments.

54
00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:48.100
First they played softly.

55
00:03:48.101 --> 00:03:53.935
Then they played loud, louder, and loudest of all.

56
00:03:53.936 --> 00:04:00.142
When the class was over, the music teacher praised everyone, especially Henry.

57
00:04:00.143 --> 00:04:07.474
"Wonderful, Henry! You did a great job playing the drum louder and louder each time."

58
00:04:07.475 --> 00:04:10.239
Suddenly, Annie had an idea!

59
00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:12.833
She hurried to Ms. Fisher to tell her.

60
00:04:12.834 --> 00:04:15.450
The teacher liked the idea.

61
00:04:15.451 --> 00:04:18.894
Then Ms. Fisher walked over to Henry and said,

62
00:04:18.895 --> 00:04:24.866
"I heard you played the drum very well today, Henry—is that right?"

63
00:04:24.867 --> 00:04:28.028
Henry smiled with pride.

64
00:04:28.029 --> 00:04:31.454
"Would you like to play the drum during the play?

65
00:04:31.455 --> 00:04:36.596
We need someone to make the sound of goats walking over the bridge."

66
00:04:36.597 --> 00:04:41.707
Henry nodded his head excitedly.

67
00:04:41.708 --> 00:04:49.228
"It's not a speaking part," Ms. Fisher said, "but we would be happy if you joined us."

68
00:04:49.229 --> 00:04:53.086
"We're going to be in the play together!"

69
00:04:53.087 --> 00:04:56.709
Annie shouted as she hugged Henry.

70
00:04:56.710 --> 00:04:59.818
The play was a big success.

71
00:04:59.819 --> 00:05:05.418
At the final curtain call, all the children lined up and bowed.

72
00:05:05.419 --> 00:05:10.072
Henry and Annie looked at each other and smiled.

73
00:05:10.073 --> 00:05:13.285
Annie gave Henry the thumbs-up.

74
00:05:13.286 --> 00:05:21.217
"I knew you could do it!" she whispered.
